Standard two-bone IK with three.js:
1. Compute the hip→target vector in the hip's PARENT space (the pelican root).
2. Set hip.quaternion so that the hip's -Y axis points along the "thigh direction" (computed from the law of cosines with a pole vector).
3. Set knee.quaternion so the shin's -Y points along the shin direction.

